@startuml
title file!readLineInto(buf) — end to end;  status reply = happens-before
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #37474F
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
actor Client #4F82C2
participant "File agent" as File #3C9C9C
participant "Buffer agent" as Buf #5FA75F

Client -> File : file!readLineInto(buf)
activate File
File -> Buf : @buf!beginFill()   (acquire lease)
activate Buf
Buf --> File : [true, fillToken]
deactivate Buf
loop until line terminator, buffer full, or EOF
  File -> File : read chunk at current position
  File -> Buf : @buf!writeBytes(chunk)   (AWAIT ack)
  activate Buf
  Buf --> File : [true, k]
  deactivate Buf
end
File -> Buf : @buf!endFill(fillToken)   (release lease)
activate Buf
Buf --> File : [true]
deactivate Buf
File --> Client : [true, [nRead, flags]]   (flags: eof, truncated)
deactivate File
note over Client, Buf
The File agent SEQUENCES: it awaits each writeBytes ack
and releases the lease BEFORE replying. The reply is the
happens-before edge; buf is unchanged and still valid.
While the lease is held, chunk-touching reads
(read / view / slice / toByteArray / validUtf8PrefixLen) return
BUFERR_FILLING for ANY caller. The File agent
releases the lease on every exit path, errors included.
end note
@enduml
